WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:05.630
Part 3 of Chilling Adventures has finally
arrived with Sabrina taking Hell under new

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:09.810
management and doubling her efforts against
dangerous new cosmic threats to Greendale.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:10.910
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:15.710
I'm Jan and in this video I'll be discussing
the mind-blowing finale of Chilling Adventures

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:19.690
of Sabrina Part 3 and how Sabrina changed
her destiny forever.

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:23.880
Plus, I'll explain what was unleashed in the
very final scene and everything to expect

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:24.880
in Part 4!

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.150
There will, of course, be spoilers ahead,
so take care if you're not all caught up.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:34.160
Part 3 of Chilling Adventures is perhaps the
most complicated season so far with Sabrina

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:39.130
using time travel to undo the apocalyptic
catastrophe that unfolds in the final two

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:40.130
episodes.

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:42.470
So, first we need to quickly recap what happened.

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:48.080
In an attempt to secure Hell against her challenger
Caliban and gain control over the three Unholy

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:52.800
Regalia, Sabrina left her family and friends
just as they were most vulnerable.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:57.320
While she was away, tragedy struck Greendale
as Father Blackwood invaded the Spellman Mortuary

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:00.149
killing Prudence, Mambo Marie, and Zelda.

00:01:00.149 --> 00:01:05.070
Meanwhile pagans abducted Sabrina's friends
to use as human sacrifices for the Great Flowering

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:07.880
ceremony to summon their Green Man god.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:12.719
And Sabrina herself was tricked into handing
over the final item of unholy regalia to Caliban

00:01:12.719 --> 00:01:16.149
who then entombed her in the Ninth Circle
of Hell.

00:01:16.149 --> 00:01:20.359
Decades later, a Sabrina from the future arrives
in the Ninth Circle to free the young witch

00:01:20.359 --> 00:01:23.109
from her stony prison by swapping places with
her.

00:01:23.109 --> 00:01:27.979
The newly liberated Sabrina returns to Greendale
with the Unholy Regalia and discovers the

00:01:27.979 --> 00:01:32.840
only person she knows left alive is Ambrose
who explains that the pagans now rule the

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:36.810
mortal realm and are harvesting human blood
to feed the Green Man.

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:41.109
Ambrose still has the time egg he stole from
Blackwood, and together they use it along

00:01:41.109 --> 00:01:45.529
with the magical energy from the Unholy Regalia
in a time travel spell.

00:01:45.529 --> 00:01:49.009
Sabrina travels back several decades to just
before the catastrophe.

00:01:49.009 --> 00:01:53.399
Knowing what's about to happen, she reaches
her family and friends before Blackwood and

00:01:53.399 --> 00:01:57.320
the pagans, and teleports them to safety at
Dorian's Gray Room.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:02.079
She also hatches a plan to defeat the pagans
which involves hedge witch Pesta using a glamour

00:02:02.079 --> 00:02:07.289
to masquerade as Ms Wardwell who's placed
in the Green Man statue as a virgin sacrifice.

00:02:07.289 --> 00:02:12.780
Pesta then infects the plant god statue, causing
it to rot and die, preventing the Great Flowering

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:14.530
from ever happening.

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:19.459
With her friends, family and Greendale saved,
and a catastrophic future averted, Sabrina

00:02:19.459 --> 00:02:23.849
knows she has to return to the Ninth Circle
of Hell because as Future Sabrina told her:

00:02:23.849 --> 00:02:26.310
"When you're done, it will be your turn."

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:27.390
"My turn to what?"

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:28.430
"To be me.

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:29.430
To do this."

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:30.430
Right now I have to go.

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:31.799
There's a promise I have to keep."

00:02:31.799 --> 00:02:36.269
But this wouldn't be Chilling Adventures without
Sabrina ignoring the rules and advice she's

00:02:36.269 --> 00:02:38.860
given, even by herself in this case.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:42.689
So she goes back to the Ninth Circle, but
with something else in mind.

00:02:42.689 --> 00:02:47.689
She intercepts a past version of herself and
warns her she's about to be tricked by Caliban.

00:02:47.689 --> 00:02:51.579
Basically, Sabrina figures that if she stops
herself from ever being trapped in the Ninth

00:02:51.579 --> 00:02:56.439
Circle, then she can avoid having to swap
back with the imprisoned Future Sabrina because,

00:02:56.439 --> 00:02:59.159
her thinking is, she never gets trapped.

00:02:59.159 --> 00:03:04.019
This creates a huge time paradox, which I'll
explain in just a moment, but to mix things

00:03:04.019 --> 00:03:09.459
up further, when the intercepted Sabrina suggests
they should merge back into a single Sabrina,

00:03:09.459 --> 00:03:14.469
our original Sabrina instead reveals she has
a plan for them both to get what they want.

00:03:14.469 --> 00:03:19.350
As a way of reconciling her dual nature and
balancing her own conflicting desires, original

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:24.189
Sabrina decides to have her cake and eat it,
by allowing a double of herself to exist,

00:03:24.189 --> 00:03:26.950
so one can be in Hell while the other is on
Earth.

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:31.170
Now by the end of Part 3, we essentially have
a set of Sabrina twins, something that was

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:34.790
foreshadowed right in the very first episode
of Season one.

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:38.719
If you've watched my previous Sabrina videos,
you'll know I theorised that when Sabrina

00:03:38.719 --> 00:03:42.969
had a vision of two babies in the woods, one
with cloven hooves and another with human

00:03:42.969 --> 00:03:46.150
feet, it hinted at Sabrina having a secret
twin.

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:50.290
Of course, that vision could have simply been
a metaphor for Sabrina's dual heritage.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:54.340
But now we see it was more than that and did
actually hint at the future existence of two

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:55.890
Sabrinas.

00:03:55.890 --> 00:04:00.459
Sabrina herself is unfazed by the implications
of this and revels in the doubling of herself

00:04:00.459 --> 00:04:04.159
when she boasts to Caliban: "Because I'm one
step ahead of you and twice the monarch you

00:04:04.159 --> 00:04:05.170
could ever be."

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:09.650
Now, if you're anything like Ambrose, you
might be rolling your eyes at Sabrina's evident

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:13.560
disregard for maintaining a stable timeline:
"If you never fulfilled your role and freed

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:16.799
yourself in the first place, the fact that
there are two of you...

00:04:16.799 --> 00:04:20.639
You have created a time paradox."

00:04:20.639 --> 00:04:21.639
"Cool."

00:04:21.639 --> 00:04:22.639
"No, not cool at all.

00:04:22.639 --> 00:04:26.650
No, the ramifications of this are horrifying
at best."

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:31.370
Ambrose is technically correct, as logically
if Sabrina has changed the future so that

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:35.669
she was never trapped, then Future Sabrina
would never have come back to free her, and

00:04:35.669 --> 00:04:40.840
our original Sabrina would never have been
able to go back in time, save Greendale and

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:41.840
intercept herself.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:45.949
Sabrina's own actions could put the stability
of her timeline in danger in something akin

00:04:45.949 --> 00:04:50.740
to "Back To The Future", the movie which Future
Sabrina referenced when she came back to set

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:52.699
original Sabrina free.

00:04:52.699 --> 00:04:57.430
In Back To The Future, Marty has to be careful
not to interfere too much with events in the

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.590
past, such as his parents getting together.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:04.620
And when he temporarily puts that in jeopardy,
his own existence becomes threatened.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:08.060
Future Sabrina already warned Original Sabrina
about this:

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:12.680
"Just remember when you're done with everything,
you have to come back to right here, right

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:16.080
now, and do what I just did to complete the
time loop.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:17.900
It's the only way to keep the realms preserved.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:20.770
If you don't, it could be chaos."

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:23.099
Chaos, of course, is to be expected in this
show.

00:05:23.099 --> 00:05:27.740
I mean, the show's acronym almost spells out
the word in English, and does so completely

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:32.139
in Spanish, a lovely little detail from creator
Roberto Aguirre-Sacasa.

00:05:32.139 --> 00:05:36.039
And as Ambrose pointed out to Sabrina:
"Everything has consequences and there are

00:05:36.039 --> 00:05:37.910
always loose ends."

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:42.130
One of those loose ends that everyone, including
Ambrose, seems to have forgotten is revealed

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:47.460
in the very final scene of Part 3, and it's
as a major consequence of altering the past.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:52.150
In this new timeline, Blackwood has actually
managed to get back both the Time Egg and

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:53.960
his twin son and daughter.

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:58.290
To understand why Blackwood now has the egg,
we need to think back to what happened when

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:02.320
he went to the Spellman house in search of
the Time Egg that Ambrose and Prudence had

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:03.590
stolen from him.

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:08.420
In the original apocalyptic timeline, Blackwood
killed Prudence, Mambo Marie and Zelda when

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:09.949
he broke into the house.

00:06:09.949 --> 00:06:15.169
But just before dying, Prudence begged Ambrose
to stop Blackwood's plan by keeping the Time

00:06:15.169 --> 00:06:16.400
Egg away from him.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:21.210
So Ambrose hid the Egg in the Greendale Mines
until Sabrina returned decades later and used

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:23.000
it for the time travel spell.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:27.480
In the new timeline, Sabrina prevents the
death of Prudence, Mambo Marie and Zelda and

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:31.740
they're teleported together with Ambrose to
safety at Dorian's Gray Room

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:35.820
What everyone forgot though is that this time
when Blackwood breaks into the house there's

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:40.449
nobody there to stop him from stealing back
the Time Egg and finding where his children

00:06:40.449 --> 00:06:41.449
are hidden.

00:06:41.449 --> 00:06:45.520
And so, with the Time Egg in hand, we see
Blackwood summon the Eldritch terrors he talked

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:50.110
about so much this season:
"Hear the birth cries of this abomination

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:52.680
and tear through the skin of reality."

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:57.130
Blackwood continues the ritual and pierces
the Time Egg with a dagger which releases

00:06:57.130 --> 00:06:58.849
an unseen monster.

00:06:58.849 --> 00:07:03.590
We hear shrieks, a snarl and some chittering
sounds, as one of the Eldritch Terrors that

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:07.590
Blackwood's ceremony summoned is let loose
in the Greendale woods.

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:12.520
To properly understand the nature of the beast
Blackwood has summoned, we need to jump back

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:16.970
to the second episode when Ambrose and Prudence
tracked Blackwood down to his hiding place

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:18.440
in Loch Ness, Scotland.

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:23.430
At the lake, Blackwood summoned a creature
he called the "Deep One", which is a term

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:27.379
that's been used for a group of water-dwelling
humanoids in the literature of H.P.

00:07:27.379 --> 00:07:28.599
Lovecraft.

00:07:28.599 --> 00:07:32.949
The "Deep One" which rises of out the lake
brings Blackwood the Time Egg that will later

00:07:32.949 --> 00:07:35.139
give birth to the Eldritch Terror.

00:07:35.139 --> 00:07:39.800
The Deep Ones are also part of Lovecraft's
Cthulhu Mythos where they're kept in check

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:41.830
by the magic of the Old Gods.

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:46.699
But with the pagans and their Old Gods defeated
in Chilling Adventures' new timeline, the

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:50.629
door is now open for Lovecraftian monsters
to enter the world.

00:07:50.629 --> 00:07:55.000
It'll be interesting to see how these Eldritch
beings and their powers are portrayed on screen

00:07:55.000 --> 00:08:00.110
in the show as, in Lovecraft's works, the
idea is that simply gazing upon a cosmic entity

00:08:00.110 --> 00:08:05.259
like Cthulhu will drive an ordinary human
insane, a concept that was also used for the

00:08:05.259 --> 00:08:08.250
monsters in the Netflix movie Bird Box.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:12.599
Blackwood references this idea somewhat when
he refers to the creature he plans to unleash

00:08:12.599 --> 00:08:13.599
as "unspeakable".

00:08:13.599 --> 00:08:18.689
These Eldritch creatures also likely come
from an entirely different dimension.

00:08:18.689 --> 00:08:23.580
In fact, Ambrose already suspected that Blackwood
was hiding in an alternate reality of sorts

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:25.889
when they were searching for him at the start
of the season.

00:08:25.889 --> 00:08:29.780
"Someone who could be anywhere in the world,
if not another dimension."

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:33.492
And Blackwood deliberately chose Loch Ness
in Scotland for his hideout because of its

00:08:33.492 --> 00:08:37.110
special location:
"Loch Ness lies atop a powerful rift along

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:38.690
the Earth's ley lines.

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:42.130
Aleister Crowley himself once harnessed its
energies for his own higher magicks.

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:46.260
A magick that could warp the very fabric of
time and space."

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:50.340
Blackwood himself seems to have dabbled in
some time manipulation while at Loch Ness,

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:54.650
because when Prudence and Ambrose find him
and his children, in the space of just a month

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:56.740
they've grown from babies into teenagers.

00:08:56.740 --> 00:09:00.710
"I've spent fifteen years inside a temporal
church of my own creation."

00:09:00.710 --> 00:09:05.080
The threat that these Eldritch monsters may
pose to not just the mortal realm but also

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:10.250
Hell if not Heaven as well is already felt
by two characters in the final episode.

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:13.550
Mambo Marie senses something wrong in the
air and tells Zelda:

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:20.160
"We must harness your coven's maternal pouvoir
for protection, and prepare them for war."

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:24.920
And over in Hell, as Sabrina prepares for
her formal coronation as queen, Lilith tells

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:27.690
her:
"Every queen must be made battle-ready.

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:29.530
Every girl must prepare for war."

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:34.620
Lilith is probably sensing the incoming inter-dimensional
threat that the Eldritch terrors represent.

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:38.720
But I also wonder whether we'll see Heaven
getting involved in this conflict.

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:42.640
Indeed, there was a little tease to this briefly
by Zelda in Part 3:

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:43.920
"Oh, honestly.

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:45.350
First Purgatory, now Hell.

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:46.350
What's next?

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:47.350
Heaven?"

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:50.760
And in the original apocalyptic timeline,
Heaven decided to intervene after the armies

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:52.710
of Hell attacked the pagans on Earth.

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:57.950
So it's quite possible we'll see another heavenly
intervention if Hell interferes in the earthly

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:00.620
clash against the Eldritch Terrors.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:04.890
Alternatively, or perhaps as well, Heaven
could get involved in trying to remedy any

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:08.890
possible instability caused by the time paradox
created by Sabrina.

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:12.080
"You have to come back..
to complete the time loop.

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:14.440
It's the only way to keep the realms preserved."

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:19.100
Fortunately, to combat this new cosmic terror
that's coming in Part 4, Sabrina seems to

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:24.060
be levelling up with each new season:
"Update: I have more power than I did before."

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:28.620
By the end of Part 3, she's able to teleport
between Hell and Earth without any special

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:32.920
spell or portal like the ones she needed from
Dorian in the first episode.

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:38.000
Another new ability she seems to have is persuasion,
where she can convince another person to believe

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.000
something.

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:42.590
Sabrina uses this with Lucy Anderson's mother
when she and Roz are looking for clues to

00:10:42.590 --> 00:10:43.590
the girl's whereabouts.

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:47.540
"You wouldn't mind if we took one of Lucy's
pinwheels with us, would you?

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:50.560
No...
you wouldn't mind at all."

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:53.080
"I wouldn't mind at all."

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:56.670
Star Wars fans might see this as a power similar
to a Jedi Mind Trick.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:58.520
"These aren't the droids you're looking for."

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:00.660
"These aren't the droids we're looking for."

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:05.190
On top of that, Sabrina's eyes go white when
she tells Caliban to back off.

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:09.710
This seems to indicate that when Lilith restored
Sabrina's powers at the end of Part 2, the

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:14.910
young witch also got back the powers she inherited
from her father Lucifer which saw her resurrect

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:18.080
from the dead, levitate and burn people alive.

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:22.210
"I am the Dark Lord's sword!"

00:11:22.210 --> 00:11:26.810
As for Sabrina's love-life, well, things didn't
turn out so great for her in Part 3.

00:11:26.810 --> 00:11:32.240
Although she rescued Nick from Hell, the after-effects
of being one with the Dark Lord made him feel

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:37.020
he could no longer be with Sabrina because
he saw too much of Lucifer, her father, in

00:11:37.020 --> 00:11:38.020
her.

00:11:38.020 --> 00:11:41.690
And when she goes to perform a cord-cutting
spell to permanently remove any feelings she

00:11:41.690 --> 00:11:44.550
has for Nick, Salem brings up Harvey.

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:50.110
Despite claiming she only loves Harvey platonically,
Sabrina quickly realises that she does still

00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:51.770
have romantic feelings for him as well.

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:55.210
So, she adds Harvey's name to the candle and
performs the spell.

00:11:55.210 --> 00:12:00.210
It's a painful moment for Sabrina and implies
she may be mostly loveless in Part 4, something

00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:04.050
that Lilith also mentioned while preparing
Sabrina to become Queen of Hell.

00:12:04.050 --> 00:12:08.170
"Let nothing touch you, let no man hold power
over you."

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:11.880
A small question I have though is whether
the cord-cutting spell actually worked if

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:14.680
Sabrina added two names to the candle?

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:18.540
Fans of Sabrina and Harvey eventually getting
back together also had their hopes dashed

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:22.820
when Sabrina herself said to Harvey that he
and Roz are destined for each other.

00:12:22.820 --> 00:12:23.960
"You guys are endgame."

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:28.500
An important change by the end of Part 3 is
that the Greendale coven no longer worships

00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:31.620
the Dark Lord, but has now become the Order
of Hecate, worshipping the Triple Goddess

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:32.620
instead.

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:36.660
Early in the season, Zelda realises it makes
no sense to continue worshipping Lucifer when

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:41.230
he's deliberately causing the coven's powers
to weaken by withholding his powers as punishment

00:12:41.230 --> 00:12:44.100
for their part in trapping him inside Nick's
body.

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:48.870
But it's not until Zelda's shot and enters
the Nether Realm, aka Limbo, that she finally

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:52.120
discovers the solution to restoring the coven's
powers.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:56.310
When she sees the three pictures of the new
moon, half-moon, and full moon during a vision

00:12:56.310 --> 00:13:00.880
of her own death, Zelda understands that only
Hecate, the three-formed goddess, has the

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:04.160
power to restore the coven.

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:10.560
"The order of Hecate, worshipping the three-in-one"
I think Hecate could come into play as well

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:15.470
in Season 4 as part of restoring the balance
between realms and defeating the Eldritch

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:16.470
Terrors.

00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:20.360
In Classical mythology, Hecate has acted as
a goddess of boundaries and as a mediator

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:22.720
between the divine and the mortal realms.

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:26.780
She was thought to have the power to either
prevent or allow dangerous spirits to pass

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:28.380
through entrances.

00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:32.550
In Chilling Adventures, when Zelda leads the
coven in prayer to the goddess, Hecate is

00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:36.800
able to bring Hilda back to the world of the
living and, conversely, she may be able to

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:40.200
help banish the Eldritch Terrors back to their
own dimension.

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:45.430
As a mediator, Hecate could also assist in
any dispute between Heaven and Hell or Earth,

